          %p
            %strong
              The following is some semblance of current research, except the stuff about the string 2-group. All errors and stupid ideas are mine -
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"} David Roberts
          %p
            For locally nice spaces (say locally contractible), it is desirable to have a functorial construction of the Whitehead tower. A shadow of a low-dimensional case of this can be seen in the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            given by Baez-Crans-Schreiber-Stevenson. Since finite-dimensional Lie groups have non-trivial third homotopy group, it is not possible to form the 3-connected cover in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
